# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EcoPilot AI — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill in the values you need.
# `.env` files are git-ignored; this template is safe to commit because it
# contains NO secret values.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# FRONTEND (bundled into public JavaScript — treat as PUBLIC)
#
# Only variables prefixed with `VITE_` are exposed to the browser.
# NEVER put a credential here: every value in this file is compiled into the
# client bundle and is readable by anyone.
#
# The Gemini API key and every other credential belong ONLY to the backend
# service that proxies agent requests. The browser never holds a secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the secure agent backend. NON-SECRET.
# Leave empty to run the deterministic, offline local tool pipeline.
# Use HTTPS in production.
VITE_AGENT_API_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BACKEND ONLY — do NOT set these in this file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These live in the deployment environment of the agent backend service
# (e.g. Cloud Run / Antigravity), never in the frontend build:
#
#   GEMINI_API_KEY        Google Gemini API key. Secret. Backend env only.
#   GEMINI_MODEL          Model id used for reasoning, e.g. a gemini-* model.
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS       Comma-separated CORS allow-list for the deployed UI.
#
# The frontend expects the backend to expose:
#   GET  {VITE_AGENT_API_URL}/health
#        -> { "geminiConfigured": boolean, "model"?: string }
#   POST {VITE_AGENT_API_URL}/agent
#        -> AgentResponse (see src/types/index.ts)
